    <!-- SOURCE GROUPS -->
    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8 space-y-12">

        <!-- 1 -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-2">Professional bodies and standards</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mb-6">The organisations that set ethical principles, competence criteria and the professional framework.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-5">
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.apa.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">American Psychological Association (APA)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The largest psychology organisation in the world. Ethical principles, practice guidelines and public information pages.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.efpa.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">European Federation of Psychologists' Associations (EFPA)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The umbrella body for national psychology associations in Europe. EuroPsy competence standards and the European meta-code of ethics.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://eaclipt.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">European Association of Clinical Psychology and Psychological Treatment (EACLIPT)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">An organisation defending the scientific basis of clinical psychology in Europe. Its position papers and the journal <em>Clinical Psychology in Europe</em> are open access.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.europsyche.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">European Association for Psychotherapy (EAP)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The umbrella body governing psychotherapy training standards and the European Certificate of Psychotherapy.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.psikolog.org.tr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Turkish Psychological Association (TPD)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">Code of ethics, professional standards and test-use competences. The consent form you sign before your first session rests on this code.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.intestcom.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">International Test Commission (ITC)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The international standard for psychological test use: test administration, translation and test security — directly binding for any scale adapted into Turkish.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 2 -->
        <div class="pt-10 border-t border-warm-tertiary">
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-2">Evidence, guidelines and research</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mb-6">The sources that tell us whether an intervention actually works.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-5">
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.who.int" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">World Health Organization (WHO)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">Mental health policy, the ICD diagnostic system and global epidemiological data.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.nice.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (NICE)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">Evidence-based clinical guidelines stating which intervention is recommended for which condition.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.cochrane.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Cochrane</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">Systematic reviews and meta-analyses. The highest level of evidence on questions of effectiveness.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.psychotherapyresearch.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Society for Psychotherapy Research (SPR)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The international scientific community studying the process and outcome of psychotherapy.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3 -->
        <div class="pt-10 border-t border-warm-tertiary">
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-2">Therapy approaches</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mb-6">The source organisations for the methods actually used at the centre.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-5">
            <li>
              <a href="https://beckinstitute.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Beck Institute for Cognitive Behavior Therapy</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The founding institution of cognitive behavioural therapy. Training, scales and practice materials.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://eabct.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">European Association for Behavioural and Cognitive Therapies (EABCT)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The European umbrella for national CBT associations and the source of its training criteria.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://schematherapysociety.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Schema Therapy Society (ISST)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The international body for schema therapy, owner of its certification and training standards. Formerly known as the International Society of Schema Therapy.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://contextualscience.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Association for Contextual Behavioral Science (ACBS)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The source for Acceptance and Commitment Therapy (ACT) and contextual behavioural science.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.europeanfamilytherapy.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">European Family Therapy Association (EFTA)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The European umbrella for systemic family therapy. A reference for family and couple work.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 4 -->
        <div class="pt-10 border-t border-warm-tertiary">
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-2">Psychodynamic</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mb-6">The theoretical and clinical sources behind the psychodynamic work at the centre.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-5">
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.efpp.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">European Federation for Psychoanalytic Psychotherapy (EFPP)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The umbrella body for psychoanalytic psychotherapy in Europe, with four sections: adult, child and adolescent, group, and couple and family.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.ipa.world" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">International Psychoanalytical Association (IPA)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The principal worldwide body for psychoanalysis. Its theoretical corpus, ethical standards and international training structure.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.annafreud.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Anna Freud</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">A centre joining the psychodynamic tradition with developmental psychology and attachment theory. The source for mentalization-based therapy and work with parents.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://tavistockandportman.nhs.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Tavistock and Portman NHS Foundation Trust</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The clinical and training institution that brought psychoanalytic thinking into public health care. Long established in systemic family work as well.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 5 -->
        <div class="pt-10 border-t border-warm-tertiary">
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-2">Trauma</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mb-6">The international and European bodies in the field of traumatic stress.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-5">
            <li>
              <a href="https://istss.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">International Society for Traumatic Stress Studies (ISTSS)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">International treatment guidelines and research in the field of traumatic stress.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://estss.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">European Society for Traumatic Stress Studies (ESTSS)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The European counterpart of ISTSS. Trauma treatment guidelines and a certification framework.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 6 -->
        <div class="pt-10 border-t border-warm-tertiary">
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-2">Children, adolescents and development</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mb-6">From academic developmental research to material written for parents.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-5">
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.escap.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">European Society for Child and Adolescent Psychiatry (ESCAP)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">Policy statements and practice standards for child and adolescent mental health in Europe.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.aacap.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">American Academy of Child &amp; Adolescent Psychiatry (AACAP)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The <em>Facts for Families</em> leaflets written for parents; a direct source for psychoeducational content.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.srcd.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Society for Research in Child Development (SRCD)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">The principal research organisation in developmental psychology. Publisher of the journal <em>Child Development</em>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://waimh.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">World Association for Infant Mental Health (WAIMH)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">Health in the first three years, attachment and the parent-infant relationship. Where SRCD gives the academic research, WAIMH gives its clinical counterpart.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://developingchild.harvard.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Center on the Developing Child (Harvard)</a>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-1">A centre translating the science of early childhood development, toxic stress and resilience into everyday language.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

